      "rev_n_1_ba3d14_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_ba3d14_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_ba3d14",
        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. The error occurs because we're trying to access `dp[i - j][0]` when `i - j` can be negative. We need to add a check to ensure we only access valid indices. Let's modify the inner loop to handle this case.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_ba3d14_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_e2472c2ea5",
        "created_at": 1794534712.3391693
      },
      "rev_n_4_1d3e70_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_1d3e70_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_1d3e70",
        "thought_text": "Use dynamic programming to build up solutions for smaller permutation lengths and combine them for larger ones.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "6741391736846632869",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794534743.4658499
      },
      "rev_n_5_4f8bc0_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_4f8bc0_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_4f8bc0",
        "thought_text": "Implement a recursive function with memoization to explore all possible permutations and count those meeting the run criteria.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "6741391736846632869",
